Spoilers follow if you don't want to know about the PYEC.  Of course,
you can always go ahead and read this and then just not wish for one.



As with other quest artifacts, you sometimes have to (#i)nvoke the
PYEC rather than (a)pplying it.  Invoking it charges any item in 
your inventory, while applying it lets you unlock stuff like any 
standard credit card.  And holding it gives you ESP, and I think 
it cuts spell damage in half.  (I'm not sure if the effects of 
two artifacts that do this are cumulative.  Does anybody know 
for sure?)   

This is a ridiculously powerful item, assuming you have the goodies
to charge up.  (Wand of Wishing (once), Wand of Death, Wand of Polymorph,
and blessed and cursed magic markers are my favorites.  And don't forget
the rings of protection, increase damage, and (for that special succubus)
adornment.)

